WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.418
ANITA KIBUNGUCHY: Increased
regulatory and compliance

00:00:02.418 --> 00:00:04.740
requirements mean that
protecting sensitive data

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.770
is top-of-mind for
many organizations.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.830
Data Catalog's integration with
Cloud Data Loss Prevention,

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:15.030
DLP, make it easy to quickly
discover PII information

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.340
and catalog it accordingly.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.410
Up next, we'll dive into how
Data Catalog helps you manage

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.091
your sensitive data sets.

00:00:22.091 --> 00:00:25.528
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:35.350
Data Catalog is a fully managed
and scalable data discovery

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:38.830
and metadata management service
that empowers organizations

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.710
to quickly discover,
understand, and manage

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:43.990
all their data in Google Cloud.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:46.810
I am Anita Kibunguchy,
and today, we'll

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:50.200
be tackling how to manage your
data assets with automatic PII

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.600
scanning capabilities
using the DLP

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.970
integration in Data Catalog.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:57.130
Knowing what's in your
data is the first step

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:59.950
to understanding
how to govern it.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:03.670
Traditionally, finding,
tagging, and handling PII

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:06.760
is an extremely manual and
time-consuming process.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:10.810
Cloud DLP integration in
Data Catalog scans your data

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:14.650
and automatically discovers
what's sensitive about it.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:17.110
The data is then
tagged and the metadata

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.860
pushed into Data Catalog.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:22.690
So you can easily search
and govern it accordingly.

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:24.580
Not only will Cloud
DLP inform you

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:27.160
if there's any PII
in your data sets,

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.320
but it will tell you
what kind of PII.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.620
Cloud DLP has over 90
types of sensitive data

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:36.790
identifiers, including social
security numbers, passport

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:39.340
numbers, birth dates, and more.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.050
Cloud DLP integration
is currently

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.570
available via API
only, but will soon

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.480
be available within
the Data Catalog UI.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.060
As a result, you can process
large amounts of data

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:52.210
quickly and automatically,
simplifying the process

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:53.990
of governing sensitive data.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:55.130
Thanks for watching.

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:57.550
And please check out all our
Data Catalog videos, or visit

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.500
our website to learn more.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.850
[MUSIC PLAYING]

